<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Northern Expedition</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1926">1926</a>–<a href="/years/1928">1928</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Northern Expedition was the military campaign of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuomintang">Kuomintang</a>'s National Revolutionary Army, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiang-kai-shek">Chiang Kai-shek</a>, to defeat the northern warlords and reunify <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. Launched from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangzhou">Guangzhou</a> in 1926, it took the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze</a> valley, split the Nationalist–Communist alliance in 1927 and entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a> in 1928, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beiyang-government">Beiyang government</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/northern-expedition.jpg" alt="Northern Expedition" width="320" height="358" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Futuretrillionaire · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Northern_Expedition_collage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
